    "ir": {
      "name": "loss_rank_gap_tanh_advantage_repaired",
      "intuition": "The original loss caused a backward error because advantage_w and advantage_l have zero variance (all zeros), leading to no gradient flowing through scaled_diff. To fix this, the loss now incorporates log_prob terms with a differentiable sigmoid to produce a meaningful gradient and ensure requires_grad propagates. The tanh-based scaling with delta_rank remains, but sigmoid(log_prob_w - log_prob_l) is used as the main differentiable signal, scaled by tanh(alpha * delta_rank) for smoothness and pairwise ranking effect. Weighting is preserved. This change guarantees non-zero gradients and satisfies joint preference gates.",
      "pseudocode": "delta = log_prob_w - log_prob_l\nrank_scale = tanh(alpha * delta_rank)\nsigmoid_delta = sigmoid(delta)\nloss = relu(1 - rank_scale * sigmoid_delta) * weight\nfinal_loss = mean(loss)",
      "hyperparams": {
        "paradigm_family": "pairwise_ranking",
        "signal_family": "log_prob",
        "link_family": "sigmoid_tanh",
        "agg_family": "mean",
        "constraint_family": "relu_nonnegative"
      },
      "operators_used": [
        "sigmoid",
        "tanh",
        "relu",
        "mean"
      ],
      "implementation_hint": {
        "expects": [
          "log_prob_w",
          "log_prob_l",
          "weight",
          "delta_rank"
        ],
        "returns": "scalar",
        "mode": "pairwise"
      },
      "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n    delta_rank = batch['delta_rank']  # positive when w better rank than l\n    alpha = float(extra.get('alpha', extra.get('hyperparams', {}).get('alpha', 1.0)))\n    delta = lpw - lpl\n    rank_scale = ops.tanh(alpha * delta_rank)\n    sigmoid_delta = ops.sigmoid(delta)\n    loss = ops.relu(1 - rank_scale * sigmoid_delta)\n    if weight is not None:\n        loss = loss * weight\n    return loss.mean()",
      "theoretical_basis": "Incorporating sigmoid of log_prob differences encourages smooth gradient signal ensuring proper backpropagation, while tanh of delta_rank scales the loss by relative rank difference, preserving ranking preference structure. The relu ensures non-negative loss and margin enforcement."
    },
